    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec adds an optional `postcode` (4 digits) to owners, validated against the city's region only when present. All 3 acceptance tests (and the full suite) are green.\n\n### Changes\n\n**Contract / schema**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added optional `postcode` (string, `^[0-9]{4}$`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so both `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response, via `allOf`) carry it. Optional (not in `required`), keeping the request contract backward-compatible.\n- `Owner.java` (entity) \u2014 added the `postcode` column + getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it in both directions by name (no mapper edits needed).\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added a nullable `postcode` column to the `owners` table (hsqldb is the test profile).\n\n**Validation (POST /api/owners pipeline)**\n- New `Postcode` util \u2014 validates only when present (null/blank \u2192 accepted). Requires exactly 4 digits, then looks up the region via the existing `LocalityResolver` (Sydney=NSW, Melbourne=VIC, Brisbane=QLD) and enforces NSW 2000\u20132099 / VIC 3000\u20133099 / QLD 4000\u20134099. A city with no known region accepts any 4-digit code.\n- `ValidateNewOwner` \u2014 calls `Postcode.validate(postcode, city)` after the existing field/telephone/email checks, throwing on malformed or out-of-range values.\n- New checked `InvalidPostcodeException` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler` + escalation YAML, responding **400** with `{\"errors\":[\"postcode\"]}` \u2014 matching the existing telephone/email error convention.\n\n**Consistency**\n- `ApplyOwner` (PUT) also copies `postcode` so an updated value persists; the PUT `ValidateOwner` uses `@Valid`, so the OpenAPI `^[0-9]{4}$` pattern enforces format there too.\n\n### Test result\n```\nTests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0 \u2014 AcceptanceTest\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```\nCovering: valid postcode stored & returned, owner without postcode accepted, and malformed postcode (`\"12\"`) rejected with 400.",
